STATE

  Version 0.2.1 on branch dev (Phase P3; Fred accepted 0.2.1 on
  2026-11-23, W14). Implemented and verified:
  - Synchronized output (DEC private mode 2026 — BSU/ESU): CSI ? 2026 h
    defers presentation in src/main.c while mutations accumulate in
    struct tl_term, CSI ? 2026 l flushes atomically, RIS resets it, and
    a 1000 ms safety deadline prevents hung programs from freezing the
    window (poll() stays timeout-free when mode 2026 is off).
  - DA2 (CSI > c / CSI > 0 c) replying \033[>1;<ver>;0c and XTVERSION
    (CSI > q / CSI > 0 q) replying \033P>|tam-last(<version>)\033\\ in
    src/term.c.
  - DECRQM (CSI Ps $ p for ANSI mode 4 and CSI ? Ps $ p for DEC modes
    1, 6, 7, 25, 47, 1000, 1002, 1003, 1006, 1047, 1049, 2004, 2026)
    in src/term.c.
  - Terminfo source terminfo/tam-last.ti defining tam-last (256-color +
    Tc) and tam-last-direct (24-bit RGB), compiled/checked with tic -x /
    infocmp -x in Makefile and installed under $(DESTDIR)$(TERMINFODIR).
  - Auto-detect TERM=tam-last in src/pty.c (including ~/.local/share/
    terminfo via TERMINFO_DIRS, falling back to xterm-256color when
    uninstalled), plus term= in tam-last.ini and --term NAME on the CLI.
  - Interactive sandbox/demo-queries (option b in sandbox/play).

